sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Viewer
  participant P as ShowDetailsPage
  participant API as API · slices
  participant CAT as Catalog · cache → TVMaze
  participant DB as MySQL
  U->>P: opens /shows/17861 (tile or deep link)
  par series header · show_details
    P->>API: GET /shows/17861
    API->>CAT: get_show
    CAT-->>API: Show · summary HTML → plain text
    API-->>P: poster · summary · genres
  and episodes · show_details
    P->>API: GET /shows/17861/seasons
    API->>CAT: list_episodes (with specials)
    CAT-->>API: Episode[]
    API->>API: group_by_season
    API-->>P: [{number, episodes[]}]
  and watched state · watch_tracking
    P->>API: GET /shows/17861/watched-episodes
    API->>DB: SELECT by user_id + show_id
    API-->>P: [{episodeId, watchedAt}]
  and comments · comments
    P->>API: GET …/comments · …/episodes/comment-counts
    API->>DB: SELECT (index show_id, episode_id, created_at)
    API-->>P: comments · count per episode
  end
  P-->>U: poster │ summary + genres · season tabs · episode tiles
  Note over P: each section loads and fails independently
  U->>P: marks an episode as watched
  P-->>U: ✓ instantly (optimistic update)
  P->>API: PUT /shows/17861/watched-episodes/1324842
  API->>CAT: get_episode · exists and belongs to show
  API->>DB: INSERT · PK (user_id, episode_id) → idempotent
  API-->>P: 200 · on failure: rollback + friendly toast
